  "verbalization": "Oblonganoside C appears to exert its biological effects through a shared pathway involving Ent-Gloeosteretriol, which acts as a target of multiple entities, including Oblonganoside C, NCI-H1734, and Tyrosine-protein kinase Fer. These entities ultimately converge on Casein kinase I isoform gamma-3, suggesting a potential mechanism where Oblonganoside C may influence the activity of Ent-Gloeosteretriol, which in turn modulates Casein kinase I isoform gamma-3. The evidence supports a hierarchical relationship where Oblonganoside C is a direct target of Ent-Gloeosteretriol, and this interaction is consistent across different targets, indicating a possible functional link. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of Ent-Gloeosteretriol as a central mediator in the signaling cascade, with Oblonganoside C potentially acting as a modulator of this pathway. The observed scores suggest a strong, consistent relationship, but further experimental validation would be necessary to confirm the exact mechanism of action.",
